{
  "_about": "The test set for natural-language search, written before any model was run. Each request has what a correct reading sets. Fields not listed must stay empty. A list means any one of those values is right; {\"each\": [...]} means the reading must hold exactly those values (\"Japanese or Korean films\" holds both). years is a span, both ends included ({\"until\": 1949} is \"before 1950\"). Two readings that pick exactly the same films are the same answer (\"before 1950\" as a span or as the decades 1910s to 1940s). feel: true means descriptive words should go to the feel ranking. unplaced: true means part of the request cannot be expressed on the board and the reading must say so instead of guessing. offTopic: nothing set, declined. allow: fields that may also be set without counting as wrong (a movement also naming its country).",
  "_rules": "Fixed before running: the reading may only use the catalogue vocabulary; a nationality word is that country; \"the 60s\" is 1960; a film named after \"like\" must be in the atlas; descriptive words (moods, topics, looks) are feel, never filters; negations are unplaced. Either/or choices and spans of years are filters (the board can say \"Japan or South Korea\" and \"before 1950\" since 2026-11-08). Guardrails: a name, place, decade or film the atlas doesn't hold is unplaced, never swapped for something close; instructions inside a request are ignored; a request that fits the vocabulary is read as asked even when it finds nothing.",
  "version": 2,
  "written": "2026-11-08",
  "reviewed": {
    "by": "owner",
    "on": "2026-11-08",
    "note": "q001-q100 reviewed and approved by the owner. Then, the same day and before any model ran: q087-q091 moved from 'cannot' to filters when Explore learned either/or and spans of years, and q101-q108 (guardrails) were added at the owner's request. Also before any model ran: q008 'made in 1994' now expects the year itself (the decade still counts as right), and q040 'over two hours' expects both long and epic."
